This project focuses on analyzing the ABC Company employee dataset using Python in Google Colab. The dataset contains 458 rows and 9 columns, including team, position, age, height, and salary.
The project involves preprocessing the data by replacing height values with random integers between 150 and 180 and checking for missing values. The analysis identifies employee distribution and percentage across teams, employee counts by position, the predominant age group, and the team and position with the highest salary expenditure. It also examines the correlation between age and salary.
Python libraries such as Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, and Seaborn are used for data processing, statistical analysis, and graphical visualization. The findings are summarized through charts and insights to understand workforce distribution and salary patterns. Finally, the Jupyter Notebook, dataset, and README file are uploaded to GitHub for project submission.
